workflows/misfeature.yaml:5:12: shell "perl {0}" is not one of the shells documented by GitHub (bash, pwsh, powershell, python, sh and cmd). it may not exist on every runner and scripts for it cannot be analyzed [misfeature]
workflows/misfeature.yaml:12:16: shell "cmd" is the Windows cmd shell, which has no formal grammar so scripts cannot be analyzed reliably, and it has not been the default shell of Windows runners since 2019. use "pwsh", "bash" or another shell instead [misfeature]
workflows/misfeature.yaml:16:16: shell "cmd /c \"{0}\"" is the Windows cmd shell, which has no formal grammar so scripts cannot be analyzed reliably, and it has not been the default shell of Windows runners since 2019. use "pwsh", "bash" or another shell instead [misfeature]
workflows/misfeature.yaml:26:16: shell "ruby {0}" is not one of the shells documented by GitHub (bash, pwsh, powershell, python, sh and cmd). it may not exist on every runner and scripts for it cannot be analyzed [misfeature]
workflows/misfeature.yaml:30:11: "pip-install" of actions/setup-python installs packages into the global Python environment, which is hard to audit and can break the resolution of dependencies. create a virtual environment and install the packages in a "run:" step instead [misfeature]
